1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,007
AquaSwarm Assignment 3 · Minimum Viable Product Dongquan Yang (dy303) · CS 549 AI for Visual Computing Real-time capture of the production build · Chromium · WebGL (Three.js)

2
00:00:06,007 --> 00:00:16,010
1 · Boids school, 100 fish
Separation, alignment and cohesion with Reynolds steering. Uniform-grid neighbour search, fixed 60 Hz simulation step, seed 549. The FPS counter is top right.

3
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:24,635
2 · Procedural swimming
Low-poly fish built in code. A vertex-shader travelling wave drives the tail; beat frequency follows each fish's speed, and the body bends and banks into turns.

4
00:00:24,635 --> 00:00:28,683
2 · Procedural swimming
Swim animation off: rigid bodies that only rotate to face their velocity.

5
00:00:28,683 --> 00:00:32,751
2 · Procedural swimming
Swim animation on again: tail beat, body bend and banking.

6
00:00:32,751 --> 00:00:43,771
3 · Click to feed
A click drops food at the water surface; it sinks. Fish within 13 units switch to Feed and seek it; the food is eaten gradually.

7
00:00:43,771 --> 00:00:50,793
3 · One food point
The MVP has a single food point: clicking again moves the food, and the feeding fish retarget.

8
00:00:50,793 --> 00:01:02,855
4 · Add the predator
One stationary predator at the tank centre. Fish that come within 8 units Flee and keep fleeing until 12 units away and at least 1 s has passed (hysteresis), so they do not flicker.

9
00:01:02,855 --> 00:01:17,868
5 · Escape has priority over food
Food dropped next to the predator. Feeding fish that get too close switch to Flee, then come back to the food once they are safe.

10
00:01:17,868 --> 00:01:25,970
6 · Recovery
Predator removed: fleeing fish slow down gradually and return to feeding or cruising.

11
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:33,988
7 · Live rule controls
Alignment switched off: fish stop matching headings and the school loses a common direction.

12
00:01:33,988 --> 00:01:41,013
7 · Live rule controls
Alignment back on, separation weight raised to 3: wider spacing between neighbours.

13
00:01:41,013 --> 00:01:45,591
7 · Pause and resume
Space pauses the simulation and the swim animation together; R resets to the seed.

14
00:01:45,591 --> 00:02:06,741
8 · Stress test: 100 → 2000 fish
The built-in test measures FPS and simulation cost per level. The simulation keeps a 12 ms per-frame budget, so under overload simulated time slows before the frame rate collapses.

15
00:02:06,741 --> 00:02:21,241
9 · Worst case: 2000 fish, one food point
All 2000 fish crowd the food, so every grid cell is full and neighbour search approaches O(N²). FPS drops and the simulated clock (top right) falls behind real time: this is the current limit.

16
00:02:21,241 --> 00:02:27,253
MVP complete One tank · 100 fish · one food point · one predator · cruise / feed / flee / recover · speed-driven tail motion Next (A4): a predator that hunts, more food and scenario presets
